;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "Logic_in_computer_science__Benji_MO"
 :source "Logic_in_computer_science__Benji_MO.pdf"
 :page 261
 :exercises "An aligned rewrite-rule array scattered by reading order: the
number and left-hand-side cells stream first, then all ten arrows, then the
right-hand column, with backward baseline jumps between the runs.  Zone
reassembly re-sorts the records by baseline row and x, so each rule reads as
one line; the rows render as display math, not as prose or a quotation.
Numbered displayed equations (rules 11-13) stand alone between paragraphs."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
